# API Requests

Always use TanStack React Query for client-side API requests and server-state management.
Always use axios as the HTTP client with TanStack React Query.
Do not use native fetch() unless explicitly requested.
Use the project's existing Axios configuration when available.
Reuse existing Axios instances/interceptors rather than creating new ones.
Use useQuery for fetching server data.
Use useMutation for creating, updating, or deleting server data.
Use query keys consistently and invalidate/refetch relevant queries after mutations.
Prefer centralized query functions/API services rather than making Axios requests directly inside components.
Do not manually implement loading, error, or caching state when TanStack React Query can handle it.
For server-side requests, use Axios with explicit timeout handling.
Keep API URLs in environment variables.
Include authentication headers when required by the backend.
Handle Axios errors appropriately and expose useful error states through React Query.
Configure shared React Query defaults through the application's QueryClient rather than duplicating configuration across individual queries.

UI Components
Prefer shadcn/ui components whenever an appropriate component exists.
Reuse existing shadcn/ui components from the project before creating new UI components.
Do not recreate a component from scratch if an equivalent shadcn/ui component is already available.
Before creating a new component, check whether shadcn/ui provides a suitable base component.
Customize shadcn/ui components using the project's existing styling and Tailwind classes rather than replacing them with custom implementations.
Maintain consistent shadcn/ui patterns across the application.
Prefer composable shadcn/ui primitives when building more complex interfaces.
If a required component does not exist in shadcn/ui, create a custom component only when necessary.
Keep custom components visually and behaviorally consistent with the existing shadcn/ui design system.
Do not introduce another UI component library when shadcn/ui can satisfy the requirement.
Reuse existing components, variants, and utilities before adding new ones.